# Global Agent Guide (example)

# Copy this to ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md (or a project's CLAUDE.md). The `@` imports pull the
# canonical rule sources into every Claude Code session, so the rules live in exactly
# one place. Pi loads the same sources through its own --append-system-prompt wrapper —
# see scripts/sync-agent-rules.sh.

## Skills

Prefer the matching skill when a request fits its trigger. Routing lives in each skill's
description; invoke the relevant skill before acting when a request matches. (List your
own skills here, or rely on a skill set such as the ones credited in the README.)

